  "term": "scotopic vision",
  "definition": "Scotopic vision is visual functioning under very low light, such as in darkness or nighttime conditions. It relies on rod cells in the retina, which are especially light-sensitive and are most responsive to wavelengths around 507 nm toward the blue part of the spectrum.",
